Changes made: each model was converted from its original safetensors files to ONNX Runtime GenAI or OpenVINO format,
with 4-bit (int4) weights, using onnxruntime-genai's model builder or optimum-intel. The tokenizer and chat template
files are copied unchanged. The weights are otherwise not changed.
Each translation model was converted from its original files to CTranslate2 format with 8-bit (int8) weights, using
CTranslate2's converter (ct2-transformers-converter); its SentencePiece files and README.md (which names its authors)
are copied unchanged. The weights are otherwise not changed.

The Picture Model Training Kit (training-kit/) downloads, when it is used, these separate programs and models; none
of them is copied into this repository:
  - PyTorch (BSD-3-Clause), Transformers, PEFT, Accelerate, Diffusers and huggingface_hub (Apache License 2.0),
    bitsandbytes (MIT), uv (Apache 2.0 / MIT), Pillow (MIT-CMU), pypdfium2 (Apache 2.0 or BSD-3-Clause; PDFium BSD-3-Clause);
  - PyAV (BSD-3-Clause) with its built-in FFmpeg libraries (LGPL 3.0 or later, as separate libraries),
    faster-whisper and CTranslate2 (MIT), ONNX Runtime (MIT), OpenCV (Apache 2.0);
  - models: Qwen3-VL (Apache 2.0), Stable Diffusion XL base 1.0 (CreativeML Open RAIL++-M) with the SDXL fp16-fix
    VAE (MIT), Stable Diffusion 1.5 (CreativeML Open RAIL-M), CLIP ViT-L/14 (MIT), faster-whisper large-v3-turbo
    (MIT), YuNet face detector (MIT).
  The wizard program (Picture Model Training.exe) includes wxPython (wxWindows Library Licence) and cytolk (MIT).
Each picture collection's licence and credit is in the kit's ATTRIBUTION.txt of every trained add-on.

